From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: refuse a link whose removal runs

Depends on 602, 603 and 822.

IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.6.3 removes the affiliated AP at the TBTT that
the AP Removal Timer names. A non-AP MLD that sets up a link to that AP
during the countdown loses the link at that TBTT. hostapd accepted such
a link in a multi-link association and in a Link Reconfiguration
Request that adds it. A driver that moved the station TX off the link
at the start of the removal (mt7996) then puts the new link station
on that link again.

Refuse a link whose removal runs with the per-link status
UNSPECIFIED_FAILURE, as the other refused links. The association or
the reconfiguration goes on over the other links. Refuse a multi-link
association that a link in removal receives, as that link would be
the association link of the station.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@ u64 hostapd_link_remove_ms(struct hostap
 }
 
 
-static bool hostapd_link_remove_pending(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+bool hostapd_link_remove_pending(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
 	return hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count ||
 		hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_offload ||
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.h
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.h
@@ -1043,6 +1043,7 @@ void hostapd_link_remove_tx_status(struc
 void hostapd_link_remove_expired(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u16 links);
 bool hostapd_link_remove_beacon_held(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
 void hostapd_link_remove_beacon_set(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
+bool hostapd_link_remove_pending(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
 bool hostapd_is_ml_partner(struct hostapd_data *hapd1,
 			   struct hostapd_data *hapd2);
 u8 hostapd_get_mld_id(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6565,6 +6565,13 @@ int ieee80211_ml_process_link(struct hos
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	if (hostapd_link_remove_pending(hapd)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: link: link_id=%u is being removed",
+			   hapd->mld_link_id);
+		status = WLAN_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED_FAILURE;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, origin_sta->addr);
 	if (sta || TEST_FAIL()) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "MLD: link: Station already exists");
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -1186,6 +1186,12 @@ static u16 hostapd_mld_validate_assoc_in
 		return WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 	}
 
+	if (hostapd_link_remove_pending(hapd)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: Link ID=%u is being removed",
+			   hapd->mld_link_id);
+		return WLAN_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED_FAILURE;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Iterate over the links negotiated in the (Re)Association Request
 	 * frame and validate that they are indeed valid links in the local AP
